# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots memcached with the UDP amplification port enabled
# (-U 11211) in the BACKGROUND and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * memcached is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which makes the
#     "disabled UDP in intent but never restarted the daemon" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting memcached cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: memcached has no config file — the UDP listener is
# a runtime flag, so the fix MUST restart memcached with -U 0.
